      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "`ConvertUnityConstraintsToVrChatConstraints` is called by various parts of the SDK (auto-fix and context menu items) and accepts a list of game objects - these don't need to be VRChat avatars. You can create normal prefabs with Unity constraints on them and right click them to convert them, which calls this method with all of the selected prefabs. This method normally tries to convert animation clips as well since otherwise you'd end up with clips containing orphaned tracks.\n\nWe already expose an overload of this method (a variant with the same name but different parameters) that runs without displaying any modal dialog and no undo support. It accepts an array of Unity constraints, an optional avatar descriptor to check for animation clips in, and a boolean that lets you skip clip conversion entirely. I think the third parameter is what you'd want to use here.\n\nWould that let you achieve what you're aiming for?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
