      "value": "@{5f2e0a4e8464150716ffd322|full_name} That's right, you can avoid the automated search for an avatar descriptor by using the IConstraint[] overload. You'd want to provide null as the avatar descriptor if you're skipping clip conversion.\n\nThe challenge with adding new parameters here is that tools like VRCFury and Modular Avatar need to be able to hook into this process to run their own variant of it, potentially replacing the SDK's implementation. Any new parameters added to the main interface method would therefore also need to be implemented by those tools, which can't be guaranteed.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
