      "value": "@{5f2e0a4e8464150716ffd322|full_name} Yes, we only try searching the avatar descriptor's animation layers when looking for clips to convert. If this is null, we fall back to searching for an Animator component with an assigned controller instead. In your case neither of those will happen since the third parameter is set to false.\n\nJust to let you know since you're writing custom code to interact with the converter already, these symbols will be renamed in a future version of the SDK since it's still technically in beta at the moment. These changes will be reflected in our documentation, but I've also summarized the renames in this other Canny here (you'll need to scroll down a bit): https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/sdk-370-beta1-please-provide-a-hook-for-supplying-additional-animation-clips-and",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
